    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena put a drop of iodine on a potato slice and it turned blue-black.\n\"There is starch,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "carbohydrate",
     "protein",
     "iodine"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Food has components: carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, fibre and water. Each has a job such as energy, growth or protection.\nTo test for starch add iodine solution: blue-black shows starch. To test for fat rub food on paper: an oily patch shows fat. Proteins can be tested with copper sulphate and caustic soda, which turn violet.\nTests help us know what a food contains."
    }
